--- !yfi/header
version: 1
namespace: edges::positions
visibility: public
--- !node &Alpha
pub port: 1
--- !node &Gamma
pub port: 3
# One endpoint that names nothing. It costs one `E0213` and nothing else: the
# three positions are the three the sequence **writes**, so `third` names
# `Gamma` and `second` names the gap rather than being quietly handed `Gamma`.
--- !edge &Gapped
pub connections: [Alpha, Nope, Gamma]
pub definition:
  first: 0
  second: 1
  third: 2
# An endpoint written inline is a node like any other; it simply has no name
# to be addressed by.
--- !edge &Inline
pub connections: [Alpha, {host: localhost}]
pub definition:
  named: 0
  anonymous: 1
# `E0225` three times. A position is a whole number written plainly, and the
# three spellings below are the three ways of almost writing one.
--- !edge &Spelling
pub connections: [Alpha]
pub definition:
  padded: " 0 "
  signed: "+0"
  leading: "00"
# `E0225`. A handle may not take one of the two names the language owns.
--- !edge &Shadowing
pub connections: [Alpha]
pub definition:
  connections: 0
# A family fixing two handles once...
--- !type &Pairwise
pub connections: [Alpha, Gamma]
pub definition:
  source: 0
  target: 1
# ...and an edge that narrows the sequence. `E0225` for `target`, reported
# about **this** node: the `definition` line it is written on is correct for
# every edge of the family that reads the sequence whole.
--- !edge &Narrowed
extends: Pairwise
pub connections: [Alpha]
# `E0223`. The declaration is inherited and nothing supplied it: the member is
# there and relates nothing, which is the failure writing no member at all is,
# with the same fix. It is not a *shape* fault, and `E0224` would send the
# author looking for a sequence they never wrote.
--- !type &Declares
pub connections:
--- !edge &Unsupplied
extends: Declares
# `E0224`, and then nothing. A member the language owns that holds the wrong
# shape has been reported once; reading the operand as an ordinary member
# naming a node afterwards would put in the image the relationship the
# compiler had just refused. A handle's value is a position for the same
# reason: it indexes a sequence and never names a node.
--- !edge &Misshapen
pub connections: ./Alpha
--- !edge &Mislabelled
pub connections: [Alpha]
pub definition:
  owner: ./Alpha
# `Alpha` is an endpoint, a base and the target of a data member, so the
# reverse index has to say which of those is a relation.
--- !node &Derived
extends: Alpha
--- !node &Points
pub at: ./Alpha
